@DISPLAY_NAME@ @VERSION@: camera control and its libraries
==========================================================

@DISPLAY_NAME@ controls cameras through libgphoto2 @LIBGPHOTO2_VERSION@, which this package includes, with
libusb @LIBUSB_VERSION@ and libltdl from GNU Libtool @LIBTOOL_VERSION@. They are free software, licensed under the
GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 or later; their license texts are next to this file:
@LICENSE_FILES@.

These libraries are separate shared libraries, which @DISPLAY_NAME@ loads when it starts camera control; it is not
linked with them. You may replace them with your own build of the same interfaces (libgphoto2's ABI 6):

  - set FLORASTACK_GPHOTO_LIBRARY to the absolute path of your libgphoto2 shared library before you start
    @DISPLAY_NAME@, and, if its drivers aren't in the folders it was built for, CAMLIBS and IOLIBS to its camera
    and port driver folders; or
  - @REPLACE@.

Source code: the source archives these libraries were built from are attached to the @DISPLAY_NAME@ @VERSION@
release, next to this package (@REPOSITORY@/releases), and the steps that built them are in @DISPLAY_NAME@'s
repository: packaging/macos/build-libgphoto2.sh for macOS, and the Flatpak manifest that xtask/src/dist/linux.rs
writes. You may also ask for the source by opening an issue at @REPOSITORY@/issues.

@DISPLAY_NAME@ itself is licensed under the MIT license or the Apache License, Version 2.0, at your option
(LICENSE-MIT, LICENSE-APACHE, NOTICE); you may modify it, and reverse-engineer it to debug your changes to these
libraries.
